<!--
  FEDA (FED Alpha) Double-Wishbone Suspension – MuJoCo XML
  Hardpoints from Project Chrono FEDA_DoubleWishbone.cpp / FEDA_PitmanArm.cpp
  Coordinate convention: X=forward, Y=right, Z=up  (Chrono Y=left → negate).

  Chassis origin at wheel-centre height (tire radius 0.499 m).
  Front axle at X=+1.651, rear at X=−1.651  (half-wheelbase 3.302/2 m).

  Suspension topology per corner:
    chassis ──hinge X (uca_*_hinge)──> uca_*
              uca_* ──ball (upright_*_ball)──> upright_*
                       upright_* ──hinge Y (axle_*)──> spindle_*  (wheel)
    chassis ──hinge (lca_*_hinge)──> lca_*
    equality connect: lca_* ↔ upright_*   (closes wishbone loop)

  TSDA spring/damper (linear approx of FEDA air spring):
    k = 76 000 N/m,  c = 38 097 N·s/m,  L₀ = 0.812 m  (same F/R)
    Geometric distance between sites at q=0 is 0.602 m; the 210 mm pre-compression
    (L₀ − d₀) models the Chrono air-spring preload (F₀ = 9 542 N) so the chassis
    sits at design ride height (z = 0.499 m).

  Pitman-arm steering (REV axis = Z, vertical kingpin):
    chassis ──motor hinge Z (steer_motor)──> pitman_arm
              pitman_arm ──ball (steering_link_ball)──> steering_link
    chassis ──hinge Z (idler_hinge)──> idler_arm
    equality: idler_arm ↔ steering_link  (closes idler loop)
    equality: steering_link ↔ upright FL/FR  (front tierods)
    equality: chassis ↔ upright RL/RR  (rear fixed tierods)

  All positions verified: wheels at z=0.499 world, springs pre-compressed 210 mm,
  all 9 equality constraints satisfied to < 1 mm at q=0.
-->
